   "summary": "Most commenters in this sample strongly oppose the proposed census rule and ask the Bureau to withdraw it. They argue the Constitution requires counting all residents regardless of immigration status, and that excluding noncitizens breaks a long-standing precedent. Many warn that dropping race, ethnicity and sexual orientation questions would hinder civil rights and voting rights enforcement, public health monitoring and planning, and that an incomplete count would cut federal funding and distort representation. Some also criticize the new residence criteria and the short comment period. A few supporters argue that only citizens and lawful permanent residents should count for apportionment and that demographic questions are unnecessary on the census form.",
