   "summary": "All of the commenters oppose the Department of Labor's proposal to make electronic delivery the default for group health plan notices. They argue that treating a failure to respond as consent is not genuine, informed choice, and that requiring people to opt out to keep paper is a burden. They say seniors, rural residents, low-income households, people with disabilities, and military families would be hurt most. They see the rule as driven by insurer cost savings and say there is no evidence that automatically switched recipients will read and understand the documents as well. They ask the Department to withdraw or reconsider the rule and keep paper as the default, with electronic delivery by opt-in.",
