   "summary": "All of these commenters oppose the proposed streamlined permitting framework for oil and gas production sites in the National Petroleum Reserve in Alaska. They argue that each project should get its own full environmental review rather than a generic one, and that public input and Tribal consultation must be kept. Many stress that the Arctic is warming fast and that more industrial development would harm wildlife, wetlands, subsistence resources, Indigenous communities and the climate. Some focus on bird habitat and the Teshekpuk Lake area, and one asks for the agency to keep its power to deny, condition or revoke approvals. The comments come from a few repeated form letters plus one detailed individual submission.",
